{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/implicitgraphs\/implicitdirectedgraph"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0..<vertexCount"},{"type":"text","text":" whose out-neighbors come from a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"closure, called on demand and never stored: an implicit graph (Boost’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"grid_graph"},{"type":"text","text":", LEMON’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"GridGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"FullGraph"},{"type":"text","text":"). It is a lawful "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"DirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":", so every generic algorithm runs"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"on it, including those that need the whole vertex set (components, centrality), with no edge"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"storage."}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/OutEdges","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/Successors"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/init(vertexCount:successors:)"],"anchor":"Initializers","title":"Initializers"},{"generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph\/DirectedGraph-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations","title":"Default Implementations"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Sequence","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Row","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":".","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:ST7ElementQa"},{"text":" == ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"For a state space with no vertex collection (an unbounded grid, a puzzle), use the closure"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"searches instead: Traversal’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"breadthFirstSearch(from:successors:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and ShortestPaths’"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dijkstraShortestPath(from:successors:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"aStarShortestPath(from:successors: heuristic:success:)"},{"type":"text","text":". For "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":" states over a finite set, number them and use"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LabeledGraph<State, ImplicitDirectedGraph<Row>>"},{"type":"text","text":"; a grid is numbered row-major."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The closure.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"successors(v)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" lists the targets of the edges leaving ","type":"text"},{"code":"v","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", once per edge, as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"any ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sequence<Int>","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (an array, a lazy filter over a fixed neighbor list), so a specialized build","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"inlines it with no type erasure. Each read of a row calls it once: ","type":"text"},{"code":"successors(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"outEdges(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"outDegree(of:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"contains(edge:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once each, ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"code":"edgeCount","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" once","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per vertex. It must return the same sequence each time it is asked about the same vertex (the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"protocol’s “asking again gives the same answer”); this is documented, not checked, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"closure that breaks it breaks every algorithm, as a mutating ","type":"text"},{"code":"==","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" breaks ","type":"text"},{"code":"Set","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Each target is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"checked to be a vertex when it is read, not when the row is formed.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Positions."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" An edge’s position is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Edges.Index"},{"type":"text","text":": its source, its rank in the source’s row,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and its target. Equality, order and hashing use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"(source, rank)"},{"type":"text","text":", unique even among parallel"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edges and self-loops; the target rides along, so "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"source(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"target(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"weight closure reading "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$0.target"},{"type":"text","text":" call nothing. There are no dense edge indices."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Codable"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":": a closure has no identity and is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Sendable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/documentation\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph"},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:14ImplicitGraphs0A13DirectedGraphV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/ImplicitGraphs\/ImplicitDirectedGraph.swift#L32"},"role":"symbol","title":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","modules":[{"name":"ImplicitGraphs"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ImplicitDirectedGraph","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure"},"relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedGraph","doc:\/\/ImplicitGraphs\/s8CopyableP"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To"}],"references":{"doc://ImplicitGraphs/documentation/ImplicitGraphs/ImplicitDirectedGraph":{"abstract":[{"text":"A finite directed graph on the vertices ","type":"text"},{"code":"0..<vertexCount","type":"codeVoi